sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: The Go client acquires credentials; the caller owns prompting and lifecycle
  accDescr: The SDK advances JSON checkpoints using an application-owned prompt callback and context. Transport must be selected explicitly and supported by both sides. Returned credentials may be stored through the configured private token store, but structural validation and Authenticate do not implement JWT verification or automatic refresh rotation.
  participant A as Calling application
  participant C as Go authclient
  participant P as Portal
  A->>C: Authenticate with context and explicit options
  C->>P: JSON identity or separate API-key exchange
  loop Password or TOTP checkpoints when selected
    P-->>C: Bound current challenge
    C->>A: Invoke caller's prompt callback
    A-->>C: Response or cancellation
    break Caller cancels
      C-->>A: Error without another portal request
    end
    C->>P: Current sandbox fields and selected transport
  end
  P-->>C: Completed credentials or failure
  C-->>A: Completed credentials for caller-owned use, or error
  Note over A,C: Renewal, admin operations, and browser Profile sessions are separate
